  "fixes": [
    "The native viewport invokes its real pointer-down host callback before emitting the first mouse byte. Shell synchronously activates the actual clicked pane, dynamically deduplicates the outer Listener, and never activates on secondary click.",
    "Human input remains dynamically restricted to the active session. A separate, equally revocable focus-loss policy permits only the exact 3-byte ESC[O system protocol report from the previous pane. Focus-in, arbitrary protocol, sendText(ESC[O), mouse, and retained human sink input retain the strict active-owner gate.",
    "Focus-loss permission defaults to the existing readOnly policy, preserves stable inputOwner, and retains mounted/session epoch/Reader/AI/read-only revocation without deactivated ancestor lookup."
  ],
